## 8. Inviolable decisions

Rules NO session or wave may contradict (each wave prompt's guardrails inherit them).
Three are STANDING (include them always, before the project-specific ones):

- **Cross-repo ownership by COUPLING, never by consumer** (detailed-plan §0): an
  artifact lives in the repo whose surface it is coupled to — schema-coupled SQL with
  the schema, app-importing scripts with the app.
- **Docs repo commit+push at every close** (execute.md §2b step 9): the docs dir is
  its own nested git repo; an unpushed logbook does not exist.
- **Code quality is a deliverable** (detailed-plan §0 · execute.md §1.9–§1.11): reuse
  is decided in planning — existing logic is consumed, logic two or more components
  need is extracted once into a shared helper both consume, and nobody improvises an
  abstraction while implementing; comments explain the WHY of non-obvious logic and
  never narrate decisions, changes or plan references (that record lives in these
  documents and in the `task.md` logbook); and every wave ends with one code-simplifier
  pass over its integrated diff before the final DoD-auto run.

